#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:323
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn; placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:307
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn; the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:239
#. Diagram label
msgid "Provision gh-pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:99
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Provisions the gh-pages branch before Pages is switched on (Task_ProvisionGhPages), derives the URL, and holds the report that follows it: \"unprovisioned\" routes back to provisioning, and \"live\", \"not-yet\" and \"unknown\" are exclusive branches of one DMN-computed gateway, so a failed probe is reported as \"unknown\", never as \"not-yet\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:98
#. Diagram label
msgid "Publish — GitHub Pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:125
#. Diagram label
msgid "Read the repository facts"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:165
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Read-only. Classifies candidates into library/ (external source) and content/ (authored here), and reports what it could not classify as its own bucket rather than forcing every file into one of the two. Its fourth section, `markers`, lists the content markers it found — sushi-config.yaml, a legacy dak.json, .bpmn processes, a beans store, library/, Lean, folio manifests — each with its paths, whether index.config.json already declares it (declared, not-declared, or unknown), and the snippet that would. `bun run cat-harness-tools/scripts/scan-repo-content.ts --json`, a plain command any agent host can run."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:313
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

