#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "scripts/pages-bootstrap.ts: check the gh-pages branch first (absent is `unprovisioned`), derive the site URL from the git remote or the layer's config (its index.config.json entry), report whether a publish workflow exists and the Pages source it needs, and optionally probe until the site answers."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:226
#. Diagram label
msgid "Seed the work plan"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Somebody said \"create a folio\": work out which request they meant, with the branch computed by a decision table that may answer \"ask\", and what has to be true before anything is written, through to a live site. \"Create a folio\" is five different requests. Gateway_Intent computes which one from decisions/folio-intent.dmn rather than letting the agent assume, and `ask` is one of the outcomes the table can return. Gateway_Live applies the same construction to publication, with `unknown` kept distinct from `not-yet`. Source of truth: this file. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/conduct/getting-started.bpmn:319
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Someone else holds the bean; this run stops without touching it."
msgstr ""

